From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Darren Shepherd <darren@obot.ai>
Date: Wed, 5 Aug 2026 15:28:16 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] test(control): pin the two key-translation rules

Both came out of the keycode bug, and neither is reachable through
GhosttyControlCore from a test - it needs a live surface - so they move into
their own translation unit alongside the settings translator.

KeycodeIsTheScanCodeNotTheVirtualKey spells out the numbers that made the bug
visible: KeyA is scan code 0x1E, and asserting it is NOT 0x41 is the actual
guard, because a virtual key is exactly what used to be passed.
ExtendedKeysCarryTheE000Prefix covers Home, the arrows and Delete, which
resolve as their numpad twins without the prefix.

ControlCharactersAreNotText is the load-bearing one: a control character in
the utf8 field does not duplicate ghostty's encoding of the key, it replaces
it, and the modes that encoding depends on are invisible from this side. It
also pins that one control character poisons the whole string rather than
being stripped, since a mixed result would short circuit just as hard.

Mutation-verified: dropping the 0xE000 prefix fails exactly
ExtendedKeysCarryTheE000Prefix, and letting control characters through fails
exactly ControlCharactersAreNotText. Both mutations had to be written to
compile - the project promotes unreferenced parameters and constant
conditions to errors, and the first attempt at each silently left a stale
test binary passing.

unitControl 42/42 -> 46/46, unitSettingsModel 159/159.
